# Architecture

patchbot is a local Go application. The CLI and web API use the same runner,
approval gate and SQLite store. The model proposes tool calls. Go code decides
whether each call and lifecycle transition is allowed.

## Package map

| Package | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `cmd/patchbot`, `internal/cli` | Entry point, flags, doctor, synchronous controls and server startup |
| `internal/config`, `secret`, `logging`, `version` | Layered TOML, credential masking, safe slog and build metadata |
| `internal/runner` | Preflight, workspace lifetime, budgets, approval, recovery and publication |
| `internal/agent` | Refine/investigate/code loops, typed approval gate, harness and recording |
| `internal/llm` | Provider interface, ordered parts, retries, schemas, models and integer pricing |
| `internal/llm/{anthropic,gemini,openai,fake,providers}` | Adapters, scripted tests and constructor wiring |
| `internal/tools` | Schema-checked file/command tools and terminal submissions |
| `internal/workspace` | `os.Root` jail, protected paths and private workspace management |
| `internal/execx` | Immutable command policy, trusted PATH, clean env and process groups |
| `internal/gitx`, `github` | Guarded local git and bounded GitHub REST client |
| `internal/store` | SQLite records, transactions, migrations and committed-event notifications |
| `internal/server` | Admission, worker lifetime, HTTP API, auth, SSE and maintenance |
| `internal/web` | Embedded templates, Vue asset, UI JS/CSS and verified vendoring command |
| `internal/testhttp`, `workspace/wstest` | Offline HTTP and jail test fixtures |

## Run lifecycle

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> queued: start
  queued --> running: preflight / clone / refine
  running --> needs_info: open questions
  running --> awaiting_approval: spec ready
  needs_info --> running: revise
  awaiting_approval --> running: revise
  awaiting_approval --> approved: exact spec approved
  approved --> running: clone / baseline / code gate
  approved --> awaiting_approval: approval invalidated
  running --> succeeded: verify / publish
  running --> failed: error or interrupted heartbeat
  queued --> failed: orphan recovered
  approved --> failed: orphan recovered
  awaiting_approval --> failed: expired
  needs_info --> failed: expired
  awaiting_approval --> rejected: reject
  needs_info --> rejected: reject
  queued --> cancelled: cancel
  approved --> cancelled: cancel
  running --> cancelled: cancel
  awaiting_approval --> cancelled: cancel
  needs_info --> cancelled: cancel
```

`phase` distinguishes preflight, clone, refine, baseline, code, verify and publish.
Clone/baseline after approval retain `approved` until the typed code gate claims
engineering questions together and record them here.

| Date | Decision | Why |
|---|---|---|
| 2026-11-10 | Go 1.27 (local 1.27.3) | Includes the GO-2026-4970 `os.Root` symlink fix the path jail depends on |
| 2026-11-10 | Remote over SSH, work on `development`, `main` only by PR | HTTPS had no credentials; keeps `main` releasable |
| 2026-11-10 | Each milestone is built in its own worktree under `../patchbot-wt/`, reviewed by the other agent plus `make ci`, merged as one commit | Lets Fable and Codex work in parallel without clashing |
| 2026-11-10 | Codex model `gpt-6.1-sol` at high reasoning; Claude side `claude-fable-5-2` | Best models available to each tool |
| 2026-11-10 | Open questions 1 to 10 from PLAN.md section 12 take the listed defaults | Owner delegated routine decisions |
| 2026-11-10 | Follow-up: `execx.stopGroup` should poll for group exit instead of always waiting the full grace period | Minor latency on cancel; not a safety issue |
| 2026-11-10 | Add `golang.org/x/text` for Unicode normalization in the path jail | Canonical-equivalent names (e.g. Hangul Jamo) bypassed protected paths on APFS; a hand-rolled table would be worse |
| 2026-11-10 | Require git >= 2.50.1 and refuse diffs over 5 MiB per file / 50 MiB total | Known clone-time CVEs in older git; git diff memory is unbounded on huge files |

## 2026-11-10: CI fixes and trusted path follow-up
- The revive `unexported-return` exception for `agent.Check` lives in `.golangci.yml`, scoped to `gate.go`,
  instead of an inline `nolint`. revive flagged it on macOS but not on Linux, so nolintlint failed CI.
- `execx` tests use `true`, not `go`, because CI runners install Go outside `TrustedPath`.
- Follow-up for M15: make `TrustedPath` configurable (an absolute-dirs-only `[limits] trusted_path`) so toolchains
  installed through asdf, mise or a toolcache can run repo tests.

## 2026-11-11: M15 release hardening

- `limits.trusted_path` defaults to the old execx path. Missing directories are
  allowed for portable configs. Existing entries must be directories without
  world writes. Validation resolves existing prefixes and symlinks, including
  dangling aliases, and checks data and actual workspace roots. The immutable
  policy supplies both executable lookup and child PATH.
- Doctor is offline unless `--online` is explicit. It reports absent fresh
  storage as a warning. It never creates a database or migrates an existing one.
  Existing pending, modified, gapped or newer migration ledgers fail inspection.
  Online probes only call provider ListModels and GitHub /user, with deadlines.
- Startup sets Unix umask 077 before work so git and child commands inherit
  private creation defaults. App-owned files and directories use 0600/0700.
  File rewrites retain only owner permission bits, including existing execute
  permission. Existing public data directories/databases are refused.
- The smoke script builds the production binary and tests its doctor command.
  The Go integration uses the same CLI dispatcher with injected fake provider,
  httptest GitHub and local bare remote. No production fake-provider flag or
  alternative approval path is added. The fixture includes its actual Go bin
  directory for setup-go/toolcache portability.
- CLI usage errors omit unparsed values. Loaded provider credentials plus
  GitHub/UI credentials are masked at the final output stream too. Registered
  credentials are masked even below the generic redactor's eight-byte threshold.
- This task does not create a release commit, tag or push. An offline cached
  scanner without a vulnerability database is not evidence of a clean scan.
if a command cannot resolve. File tools use an `os.Root` jail and protect `.git`,
`.env*`, `.github/workflows` and configured paths. Huge diffs are refused above
5 MiB per file or 50 MiB total.

The server runs two jobs with sixteen queued by default. Excess admission gets
HTTP 429. A limit reached with changes can produce a draft salvage PR after
harness tests. Cancellation, authentication errors and refusals publish nothing.
No diff means no PR. Missing tests or failed verification produce a draft.

Registered credentials of at least eight characters, including `PATCHBOT_UI_TOKEN`,
are masked before model input, persistence and CLI/API output. Shorter values
are ignored for substring masking; `config check` and `doctor` warn without
printing them. Redaction preserves harness phases, statuses and JSON/TOML keys.
Adapter request deadlines are retryable `unavailable` errors while caller
cancellation or deadlines stop retries.

## FAQ

**Can it work on any repository?** Only allowlisted repositories. The model
cannot add repositories or commands. Use ones you trust.

**Does a dry run spend money?** It can. It uses your configured model and runs
real tests. `make smoke` uses fakes and costs nothing.

**Does approval prove the patch is safe?** It approves the spec. Read the diff,
harness results and PR. The agent's claims do not replace the harness or review.

**Can I run it unattended or on a hostile repo?** This release is for one local
operator. It has no container isolation, webhooks, durable worker queue, login or
deployment system. Hostile repository code is outside its protection boundary.

**What happens after a crash?** Expired heartbeats become interrupted failures
at startup or maintenance. Retry creates a new run. A push followed by a failed
PR request needs manual inspection; there is no publication reconciliation.

## Development and license

`make ci` checks formatting, vet, lint, race tests and a CGO-free build.
`make smoke` runs offline acceptance. Go and lint caches can be put under
`/private/tmp` in a restricted workspace. CI also runs govulncheck with its live
vulnerability database. No real provider credentials are needed by tests.

See [architecture](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [security](SECURITY.md),
[contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md) and the [changelog](CHANGELOG.md).
Licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE).
